From 900921ee1424c50058ef1af80177e9b38fa8bfb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:01:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] gui: migrate data from the legacy
 ProgramData\NimbusBackup folder

The data directory moved from ProgramData\NimbusBackup to the
brand-neutral ProgramData\ProxmoxBackupClient without a migration, so
upgraded installs started with an empty config and no scheduled jobs.

On first access to the data directory, copy config.json,
scheduled_jobs.json, job_history.json and api-token from the legacy
folder. Files are created no-clobber (temp file + hard link), so a
concurrent GUI/service run can never replace a file already migrated or
edited since. Completion is recorded by a marker file written only after
every copy succeeded, so an interrupted migration is retried on the next
start even if a config was saved in between. Once done, a
COPIED-TO-ProxmoxBackupClient.txt note is also left in the legacy folder
(where, when, which version); it marks the folder as copied, so the
migration never runs again, even if the new folder is deleted later. The legacy folder is kept
(downgrade-safe); logs and the restore cache are skipped. The
scheduler's job/history paths now reuse getConfigDir() instead of
duplicating it, so they get the migration too.
---
 gui/config.go              |   3 +
 gui/legacy_datadir.go      | 129 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gui/legacy_datadir_test.go | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gui/scheduler.go           |  50 +++-----------
 4 files changed, 264 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gui/legacy_datadir.go
 create mode 100644 gui/legacy_datadir_test.go

